To rank well and convert visitors into leads, these programmatic city pages shouldn't just be thin placeholders. They need to provide a complete "landing page experience" tailored to a B2B audience (purchasing managers, project leaders, calculation departments).

Here is the ideal content structure I suggest adding to these pages over time (which we can easily structure into the CitySEO JSON block later):

1. The Hero Section (Intent & Urgency)
H1 (Title): Betrouwbare Onderaannemers & Bouwpersoneel in [City]
Subheadline: Address their main pain point. “Heeft u op korte termijn extra capaciteit nodig voor uw bouwproject in de regio [City]? Wij leveren direct inzetbare, gescreende vakmensen voor grote aannemers.”
Call to Action (CTA): Vraag direct capaciteit aan (Request capacity now)
2. Available Trades (What can they hire?)
List the specific types of workers you supply. Google loves semantic keywords.

Vakgebieden beschikbaar in regio [City]:
Ruwbouw (Metselaars, Bekisters, IJzervlechters)
Afwerking (Stukadoors, Schilders, Tegelzetters)
Technieken (Elektriciens, Loodgieters, HVAC)
Machinisten (Kraan, Graafmachine)
3. Local Trust & Logistics (Why Choose You)
Explain why working with you in that specific region makes sense.

Lokale Kennis: “Onze onderaannemers zijn lokaal gehuisvest of bereid tot verblijf in de buurt van [City], waardoor u geen last heeft van vertragingen.” (Local presence prevents delays).
Administratieve Ontzorging: “Wij regelen alle wettelijke verplichtingen (Limosa, A1, Checkinatwork) zodat u zich kunt focussen op de bouw.” (Handling administration/compliance).
7-Dagen Proefperiode: Mention your 7-day trial week (from your main site's messaging).
4. Regional Breadcrumbs / Surrounding Areas
To boost local SEO, it helps to mention the surrounding province.

"Niet alleen in [City] centrum, maar ook actief op werven in de omliggende gemeenten en de rest van de provincie." (Active not just in the city center, but surrounding municipalities).
5. FAQs (Frequently Asked Questions)
Google often pulls FAQ content into the search results. Include 3 questions:

Hoe snel kunnen onderaannemers starten in [City]? (How fast can they start?)
Zijn alle documenten in orde voor werven in België? (Are all documents compliant?)
Kan ik ook ploegen inclusief meewerkend voorman inhuren? (Can I hire teams with a working foreman?)
6. Final Call to Action
"Klaar om uw werf in [City] te versterken? Bespreek vandaag nog uw personeelsbehoefte met ons team."
Next Steps Strategy: You don't need to write 100% unique text for every single city. You can write one really strong version of the structure above, put it in the nl.json / fr.json templates, and use the {city} variable throughout it. Google understands that programmatic SEO pages share structural content, as long as the local relevance and intent match what the user is searching for!